BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (  A traveler who could see both gardens spoke: "You each believe the other has failed you. But t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    he fog distorts everything. She poured three buckets-you received one. You returned half of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    one-she saw three drops.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  "The cruelest trick of fog isn't that it hides-it's that it makes both parties feel justified ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    in withdrawal. You each think you're adapting wisely to the other's betrayal. In truth, you') Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    re both responding to phantoms.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  "True wisdom in fog isn't just adaptation-it's humility. Consider: might the fog deceive YOU a) Tj ET
